#: ../../plugins.rst:4
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "A plugin adds a service to Guidedog. A build plugin can transform "
#| "source text, transform a rendered HTML page, or supply static files. A "
#| "publisher sends a finished site to a destination. These services use "
#| "ordinary Odin procedure tables."
msgid ""
"A plugin adds a service to Guidedog. A build plugin can transform source "
"text, transform a rendered HTML page, or supply static files. A publisher "
"sends a finished site to a destination. Both are ordinary Rust traits "
"from the ``gd-plugins`` crate. We implement one once. The same value can "
"be linked into a custom ``guidedog`` binary or served as a separate "
"program."
msgstr ""
"Plugin, Guidedog में एक सेवा जोड़ता है। Build plugin मूल पाठ या तैयार "
"HTML पेज को बदल सकता है और स्थिर फ़ाइलें दे सकता है। Publisher तैयार साइट "
"को उसके गंतव्य पर भेजता है। ये सेवाएँ Odin की सामान्य procedure tables का "
"उपयोग करती हैं।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:10
msgid ""
"This chapter builds a product badge. It replaces ``{{product}}`` in "
"source text, adds a label to HTML pages, and supplies the label's CSS. "
"GitHub Pages then shows how the same plugin foundation supports a service "
"with external effects."
msgstr ""
"इस अध्याय में उत्पाद का badge बनाएँगे। यह मूल पाठ में ``{{product}}`` की "
"जगह नाम रखता है, HTML पेज में लेबल जोड़ता है और उसका CSS देता है। फिर "
"GitHub Pages से समझेंगे कि यही आधार बाहरी सिस्टम पर असर डालने वाली सेवा "
"को कैसे संभालता है।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:14
msgid "1. Understand the boundary"
msgstr "1. इंटरफ़ेस की सीमा समझें"

#: ../../plugins.rst:17
msgid ""
"A build plugin implements ``gd_plugins::BuildPlugin``. Its "
"``process_source``, ``process_html`` and ``collect_assets`` methods are "
"optional. The default methods mean the service is absent (text passes "
"through, no assets). ``load`` reads the plugin's configuration into the "
"value itself. Dropping the value releases what it holds. The host owns "
"the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../plugins.rst:25
msgid ""
"Source hooks precede parsing. HTML hooks and generated assets enter "
"staging. Publication follows a successful build."
msgstr ""
"Source hooks parsing से पहले चलते हैं। HTML hooks और बने हुए assets "
"staging में जाते हैं। प्रकाशन सफल बिल्ड के बाद होता है।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:25
msgid "Build services precede publication."
msgstr "बिल्ड सेवाएँ प्रकाशन से पहले चलती हैं।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:52
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Source hooks run before parsing each primary RST or Markdown document. "
#| "They apply to PDF and text builds too. Includes remain the engine's "
#| "responsibility. HTML hooks receive complete pages, including generated "
#| "indexes and additional pages. Generated assets belong to HTML builders "
#| "and live below ``_static/plugins/ID/``. The host collects them once "
#| "during plugin setup, before reading documents. They are fixed for that "
#| "build; source and HTML hooks cannot add later assets."
msgid ""
"Source hooks run before parsing each primary RST or Markdown document. "
"They apply to PDF and text builds too. Includes remain the engine's "
"responsibility. HTML hooks receive complete pages, including generated "
"indexes and additional pages. Generated assets belong to HTML builders "
"and live below ``_static/plugins/ID/``. The host collects them once "
"during plugin setup, before reading documents. They are fixed for that "
"build. Source and HTML hooks cannot add later assets."
msgstr ""
"सोर्स हुक हर मुख्य RST या Markdown दस्तावेज़ के पार्स होने से पहले चलता "
"है, PDF और टेक्स्ट में भी। include इंजन पढ़ता है। HTML हुक को इंडेक्स और "
"अतिरिक्त पृष्ठ समेत पूरा HTML मिलता है। बने एसेट केवल HTML के लिए "
"``_static/plugins/ID/`` में हैं। होस्ट दस्तावेज़ पढ़ने से पहले प्लगइन "
"सेटअप में इन्हें एक बार लेता है। वे उस बिल्ड में तय रहते हैं; बाद के हुक "
"और एसेट नहीं जोड़ सकते।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:59
