msgid ""
"A ``Plugin`` is build hooks or a publisher, never both. Normal builds "
"cannot invoke a publishing service. A plugin reaches a build in one of "
"two ways:"
msgstr ""
"Plugin table में build hooks या publisher में से एक होता है, दोनों नहीं। "
"सामान्य बिल्ड publishing service को नहीं बुला सकता। स्थापित plugins "
"भरोसेमंद native programs होते हैं। उन्हें स्पष्ट रूप से register करने पर "
"executable का SHA-256 तय होता है। यह sandbox नहीं है।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:62
msgid "Linked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../plugins.rst:63
msgid ""
"A custom ``guidedog`` binary compiles the plugin crate in and passes its "
"plugins to the command line with ``gd_cli::run_with``. Rust has no stable "
"ABI, so there is no loading of dynamic libraries. Linked code is trusted "
"like the rest of the binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../plugins.rst:67
msgid "Served"
msgstr ""

#: ../../plugins.rst:68
msgid ""
"The plugin crate's small binary calls ``gd_plugins::serve_plugin``. We "
"register it with ``guidedog plugin register``, which pins its SHA-256. "
"Then it runs as a child process per build, behind a bounded JSON Lines "
"protocol. A crash or stall becomes a diagnostic. Registration is "
"explicit, and it is not a sandbox: an installed plugin is a trusted "
"program."
msgstr ""

