#: ../../plugins.rst:317
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Its ``Publisher`` supplies ``load``, ``plan``, ``publish``, ``status`` "
#| "and ``recover``. A session owns configuration and credentials. A "
#| "snapshot owns checked site files. A plan compares that snapshot with a "
#| "target baseline. A result reports the verified outcome. Release each "
#| "owner with its matching SDK procedure."
msgid ""
"A publisher implements ``gd_plugins::Publisher`` and is wrapped with "
"``Plugin::publisher``. Its methods are ``info``, ``load``, ``plan``, "
"``publish``, and optional ``status`` and ``recover``. A session holds "
"configuration and credentials. A ``Snapshot`` freezes the checked site "
"files. A ``Plan`` compares that snapshot with a target baseline. An "
"``Outcome`` reports the verified result. These are ordinary values, and "
"there is nothing to release."
msgstr ""
"उसका ``Publisher``, ``load``, ``plan``, ``publish``, ``status`` और "
"``recover`` देता है। Session configuration और credentials का owner है। "
"Snapshot जाँची हुई साइट फ़ाइलों का owner है। Plan snapshot की तुलना "
"target की baseline से करता है। Result सत्यापित परिणाम बताता है। हर owner "
"को उसकी संबंधित SDK procedure से मुक्त करें।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:324
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Follow ``examples/pages-publisher/main.odin`` into ``lib/pages``: "
#| "configuration and machine binding establish authority; planning reads "
#| "the target; publishing writes a durable journal before one conditional "
#| "Git push; status and recovery settle the outcome. Nothing in a source "
#| "or HTML callback grants publication authority."
msgid ""
"Start with :download:`publisher.rs <_static/repository/publisher.rs>` "
"(``crates/gd-plugins/examples/publisher.rs``), a working publisher that "
"replaces a local folder whole. Then follow the GitHub Pages publisher in "
"``crates/gd-pages``. Configuration and machine binding establish "
"authority. Planning reads the target. Publishing writes a durable journal "
"before one conditional Git push. Status and recovery settle the outcome. "
"Nothing in a source or HTML hook grants publication authority. ``guidedog "
"publish --publisher=ID --config=FILE`` builds the project and runs a "
"publisher. ``--dry-run`` stops after the plan."
msgstr ""
"``examples/pages-publisher/main.odin`` से ``lib/pages`` तक implementation "
"देखें। Configuration और machine binding अधिकार तय करते हैं। Planning "
"target पढ़ती है। Publishing एक conditional Git push से पहले टिकाऊ journal "
"लिखती है। Status और recovery परिणाम स्पष्ट करते हैं। Source या HTML "
"callback को publishing का अधिकार नहीं मिलता।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:333
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "A remote acceptance is not a live deployment. ``Accepted`` and "
#| "``Pending`` return 6; an uncertain write returns ``Unknown`` and 7, "
#| "with status or recovery directions. Never retry an uncertain write "
#| "blindly. See :doc:`howto/github-pages` for the complete user workflow, "
#| "and the API reference for :odin:type:`~plugins.Publisher`."
msgid ""
"A remote acceptance is not a live deployment. ``Accepted`` and "
"``Pending`` return 6. An uncertain write returns ``Unknown`` and 7, with "
"status or recovery directions. Never retry an uncertain write blindly. "
"See :doc:`howto/github-pages` for the complete user workflow."
msgstr ""
"Remote acceptance का अर्थ live deployment नहीं है। ``Accepted`` और "
"``Pending`` का exit status 6 है। अनिश्चित write में ``Unknown`` और 7 आते "
"हैं तथा status या recovery के निर्देश मिलते हैं। अनिश्चित write को बिना "
"जाँच दोबारा न भेजें। पूरे workflow के लिए :doc:`howto/github-pages` और "
"API reference में :odin:type:`~plugins.Publisher` देखें।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:338
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "9. Version and distribute the contract"
msgid "10. Version and distribute the contract"
msgstr "9. Contract का version तय करें और वितरित करें"

#: ../../plugins.rst:341
msgid ""
"The build-plugin interface (``PLUGIN_API_VERSION``) is 1.0 and uses "
"protocol ``guidedog-build-plugin`` 1.0. The publisher interface "
"(``API_VERSION``) is 1.1 and keeps ``guidedog-publisher`` protocol 1.0. "
"These are separate contracts. The wire format is the one that programs "
"built with the Odin SDK speak, so registered programs from earlier "
"releases keep working. Product versions are separate from interface "
"versions. New hooks arrive as trait methods with \"absent\" defaults, and "
"host-made inputs are ``#[non_exhaustive]``, so a new field does not break "
"a plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../plugins.rst:349
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Register each rebuilt executable deliberately. ``guidedog plugin "
#| "inspect ID`` shows its kind and declared hooks. The public catalog "
#| "describes plugins; it does not download, install or run them. Custom "
#| "markup readers and renderers still use the compiled ``core.Registry`` "
#| "API. Installed custom directives, roles and builders are not part of "
#| "this build-hook interface."
msgid ""
"Register each rebuilt program deliberately, because its checksum changes. "
"``guidedog plugin inspect ID`` shows its kind and declared hooks. The "
"public catalog describes plugins. It does not download, install or run "
"them. Custom markup readers, renderers, directives and roles are not part "
"of this interface. They use the ``guidedoc::Registry`` API in a program "
"that embeds the engine."
msgstr ""
"हर दोबारा बने executable को सोच-समझकर register करें। ``guidedog plugin "
"inspect ID`` उसका प्रकार और घोषित hooks दिखाता है। सार्वजनिक catalog "
"plugins का विवरण देता है, उन्हें डाउनलोड, स्थापित या चलाता नहीं। Custom "
"markup readers और renderers अब भी compiled ``core.Registry`` API का उपयोग "
"करते हैं। Install किए जाने वाले custom directives, roles और builders इस "
"build-hook interface का हिस्सा नहीं हैं।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:355
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "10. Check a plugin before registering it"
msgid "11. Check a plugin before registering it"
msgstr "10. Register करने से पहले plugin जाँचें"

#: ../../plugins.rst:358
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "``guidedog plugin check PATH --project=DIR --config=FILE`` exercises a "
#| "build plugin without changing the registry. Registration runs the same "
#| "checks automatically: two fresh loads, repeated source and HTML "
#| "results, generated asset validation and cleanup. ``--timeout=SECONDS`` "
#| "defaults to 60 per process request. Supply a real configuration when "
#| "the plugin needs one. Relative configuration paths resolve from "
#| "``--project``; its default is the current directory."
msgid ""
"``guidedog plugin check PATH --project=DIR --config=FILE`` exercises a "
"build plugin without changing the registry. Registration runs the same "
"checks automatically: two fresh loads, repeated source and HTML results, "
"generated asset validation and cleanup. ``--timeout=SECONDS`` defaults to "
"60 per process request. Supply a real configuration when the plugin needs "
"one. Relative configuration paths resolve from ``--project``, whose "
"default is the current directory."
msgstr ""
"``guidedog plugin check PATH --project=DIR --config=FILE`` बिना registry "
"बदले build plugin जाँचता है। Registration भी यही करता है: दो नए loads, "
"दोहराए source और HTML results, assets का validation और cleanup। "
"``--timeout=SECONDS`` का default हर process request के लिए 60 है। ज़रूरत "
"हो तो असली configuration दें। Relative configuration paths का आधार "
"``--project`` है, जिसका default वर्तमान directory है।"

#: ../../plugins.rst:365
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Passing checks demonstrates interoperability, not a proof of safety. "
#| "Guidedog keeps checking every runtime response and runs installed "
#| "plugins in separate processes. A crash, bounds failure or stalled "
#| "process becomes a diagnostic and cannot publish an incomplete "
#| "generation. Earlier publisher compatibility is no longer a release "
#| "requirement; qualification checks demonstrate interoperability across "
#| "process boundaries, while directly linked native callbacks remain "
#| "trusted code."
msgid ""
"Passing checks shows that the plugin works with Guidedog. It is not a "
"proof of safety. Guidedog keeps checking every runtime response and runs "
"installed plugins in separate processes. A crash, bounds failure or "
"stalled process becomes a diagnostic and cannot publish an incomplete "
"generation. Linked plugins remain trusted code."
msgstr ""
"जाँच पास होना साथ काम करने का प्रमाण है, पूरी सुरक्षा का नहीं। हर रनटाइम "
"उत्तर फिर भी जाँचा जाता है और इंस्टॉल किए प्लगइन अलग प्रक्रिया में चलते "
"हैं। क्रैश, सीमा उल्लंघन या रुकना डायग्नोस्टिक बनते हैं; अधूरा संस्करण "
"प्रकाशित नहीं होता। पुराने पब्लिशर की संगतता अब शर्त नहीं; सीधे जुड़े "
"नेटिव कॉलबैक अब भी भरोसेमंद कोड हैं।"

